        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 1 R code file.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1L, File = \"fake_dep.R\", \"Runs after\" = \"—\", \n    Basis = \"none\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "To run against the Psych-DS layout, 0 referenced data paths would be rewritten to their new locations.",
          "#### Missing inputs",
          "Every data file the code reads is either produced by an earlier script or present in the repository.",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the Psych-DS layout, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 1 script: 0 ran without error, 0 errored, 0 timed out, 0 were skipped (inputs unavailable), 1 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, and 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"fake_dep.R\", Outcome = \"dependency_unavailable\", \n    Detail = \"dependency_unavailable\", \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "**Dependency-unavailable errors**",
          "**1 script could not run because its own dependency is unavailable** — the package failed to install from both live CRAN and the CRAN Archive (or a GitHub/URL source could not be resolved). This is an infrastructure limitation, not a defect in the paper's code, so it does **not** force the traffic light red.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"fake_dep.R\"), row.names = c(NA, -1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — fake_dep.R (dependency_unavailable)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> x <- 1\n> stop(\"there is no package called 'oddpkg'\")\n````\n**Messages / errors (stderr):**\n````\nError in eval(e, envir = env) : there is no package called 'oddpkg'\n````\n\n:::\n",
          "Dependencies were installed into a throwaway library before running: 2 succeeded, 2 failed. notapkg123, oldpkg, oddpkg, fine were installed.",
